   FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:3028](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3028), [scripts/upgrade.sh:3046](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3046)  
   Concrete failure: `_refresh_schema_doc` hashes and copies through destination symlinks without checking the leaf or parents. A supported `install.sh --link` installation creates schema-file symlinks ([scripts/install.sh:898](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/install.sh:898)). Upgrading it from a newer checkout can recognize the old referent as a prior generation and `cp` new content through the symlink, modifying the old source checkout outside the adopter target. A symlinked `.claude/plans` ancestor gives the same escape.  
   Minimal fix: reject symlinked ancestors and leafs before reading or writing. For provenance-authorized LINK records, replace the link itself atomically; never overwrite its referent. Add link-mode and hostile-ancestor positive controls.

