.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-611-# `--stable` would let an rc.N ship a post-review commit and then become the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-612-# unreviewed baseline the GA is promoted from.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-613-#
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-614-# THE LOCAL ASSERT IS NOT ENOUGH — say it out loud. A tag signed by hand skips
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:615:# this driver entirely, and the pair-rail step 15 recomputes inputs_hash only
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:616:# over `pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt`, which deliberately EXCLUDES the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-617-# bump surfaces (including them would make every legitimate bump change the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-618-# inputs_hash and break the verdict replay). The same restricted-delta assert
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-619-# therefore goes SERVER-SIDE into `.github/workflows/release.yml` in PLAN-166
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-620-# W1. release.yml is canonical: it changes under the GPG ceremony, not here.
