   130	    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
   131	    # PLAN-161: 5 -> 8 — headroom for the two upgrade oracles (each runs
   132	    # full install + upgrade legs against fixture adopter repos).
   133	    # PLAN-166 F4: 8 -> 20. MEASURED, not guessed. The parity e2e runs 2 full
   134	    # install legs + 1 upgrade leg PER ceremony mode, and the positive control
   135	    # runs the same again with a planted divergence: 12 install/upgrade
   136	    # operations added to this job. Local wall time (Darwin arm64, 16 cores,
   137	    # 2026-08-05): gate 122s + control 118s = 240s. A 2-core ubuntu-latest
   138	    # runner is the usual 2-3x slower, i.e. 8-12 min of NEW work on top of the
   139	    # ~5 min this job already spent. 15 would sit inside the noise band, and
   140	    # the perf-gate N=20 flake (PLAN-159) was exactly that mistake. Re-tighten
   141	    # once real CI runs give a p95.
   142	    # PLAN-166 F3 (assembler): 20 -> 25. The spec-ownership e2e adds 4 more
   143	    # installs + 3 upgrades (S1-S8; ~3-4 min local per the W1-C measurement),
   144	    # i.e. up to ~8-10 more CI minutes at the same 2-3x factor. Same
   145	    # anti-flake sizing rule as the F4 bump above.
   146	    # PLAN-177 W1 (CF-9): 25 -> 32. The night-mode efficacy e2e adds 3 installs
   147	    # + 2 upgrades. MEASURED, not guessed: 2m06s wall on Darwin arm64 (16
   148	    # cores, 2026-08-13), reproduced across two runs. At the same 2-3x runner
   149	    # factor this workflow already sizes with, that is 4-7 CI minutes, so +7.
   150	    # A job-level timeout that clips a green run reports as `cancelled` on an
   151	    # innocent step (the S2xx lesson), so the margin stays deliberate.
   152	    timeout-minutes: 32
   153	    permissions:
   154	      contents: read
   155	    steps:
   156	      - name: Checkout
